## Material Selection & Mechanical Specifications: HERMESPIDER-12## 1. Central Core Chassis & Inner Enclosure (基殻・密閉空間)
To safeguard the 5-core centralized computing unit and high-capacity battery, the inner container requires extreme torsional rigidity, IP68 hermetic sealability, and high thermal conductivity.

* Primary Material: Aluminum Alloy (Al-Si-Mg system) / ISO AlSi10Mg (Processed via Precision Die-casting or Selective Laser Melting 3D Printing).
* Rationale: Combines structural lightness with a high thermal conductivity (≈ 110 W/m·K) to act as a direct heat sink for the 5-core CPU array, avoiding thermal runaway within the sealed IP68 cavity.
* Sealing Interfaces (Gaskets): Fluorosilicone Rubber (FVMQ) / ASTM D1418.
* Rationale: Outperforms standard NBR or silicone. It maintains stable elastic recovery and sealing torque under extreme temperature fluctuations, structural fuel/oil contamination, and high mud pressure.

## 2. Dynamic Articulated Legs & Links (可動脚・リンク機構)
The 12-leg operational mechanism (36 DoF total) undergoes aggressive impact loads during the "0.001-Second Ultra-Fast Bracing Reflex" and high crushing forces from debris or panicked human grab.

* Hip & Knee Structural Links: Carbon Fiber Reinforced PEEK (CF30-PEEK) / ISO 1043 PEEK-CF30.
* Rationale: 30% carbon-fiber-reinforced Polyetheretherketone. It provides a specific strength matching structural aluminum but at a much lower density (≈ 1.45 g/cm³ vs. Aluminum 2.7 g/cm³). This is crucial for keeping the total leg assembly weight under the 3kg total target limit while resisting elastic deformation.
* Threshold Springs (Physical Filter): Titanium Alloy (Ti-6Al-4V Grade 5) / ASTM B348.
* Rationale: Offers the highest strength-to-weight ratio among spring-capable materials. It handles continuous high-frequency displacement without fatigue failure and resists corrosion in acidic/hazardous post-disaster floodwaters.

## 3. Outer Floating Protection Shell (外殻・アウターシェル)
The outer shell must absorb localized impacts (falling concrete chips, pounding from victims) and distribute the load away from the inner core chassis.

* Primary Shield Dome: Polycarbonate/Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene Blend (PC-ABS) / ISO 2580.
* Rationale: Combines the extreme impact toughness and heat resistance of PC with the high processability and dimensional stability of ABS. It acts as a sacrificial flexural barrier.
* Dynamic Pressure Array Coating: Polyurethane Elastomer (TPU) Overmold / ISO 18064.
* Rationale: A shore hardness of 80A–90A provides a soft, non-threatening touch for human interaction, dampens mechanical impact vibrations before they reach the internal piezoceramic sensors, and prevents PC-ABS fracturing.

## 4. Foot-End Topology & Anchoring Interface (足端・接地面)
The foot end requires high friction on slick oil/mud while allowing micro-suction on smooth submerged surfaces.

* High-Traction Tread Pad: Fluorocarbon Elastomer (Viton / FKM) / ASTM D1418.
* Rationale: Retains high friction coefficients (μ > 0.6) even when saturated with industrial oils, hydraulic fluids, or organic mud, preventing locomotive slippage.
* Micro-Suction Pad Array (Geckopad): Polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE) Nano-coated Silicone Micro-pillars.
* Rationale: The core design utilizes van der Waals forces and micro-pressure differentiation for underwater anchoring. The PTFE nano-coating prevents self-adhesion and mud clogging during the lift-off phase, guaranteeing clean detachment.

